From bbd69cda2cf65b0356aeaea5a0b3082593199da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:54:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] wip/kv-residency: A3 -- --fit sizing + reporting of the
 window, the pinned-RAM gate, and three slide bugs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Item 1 (--fit): `LLAMA_KV_RESIDENT_CELLS=auto` leaves the window to `--fit`, which knows both budgets (the
VRAM left after the arena/slab reserve, and the pinned-RAM ceiling).  It measures the KV's own bytes from the
region buffer type, sizes W, hands it down through a process global the KV cache reads at creation, keeps the
user's `-c` when the windowed config fits (instead of shrinking it), and reports the split plus the modelled
per-token cost at the calibrated link rate.  `memory_breakdown()` reports only the RESIDENT bytes against the
device buffer type and the spill against the CPU one, so the memory table and `--fit` agree.

Item 3 (RAM gate): LLAMA_KV_SPILL_RAM_PCT (85 % of MemAvailable, 0 disables) clamps W at creation -- the
worst-case spill, shared by every cache in the process -- and the run-time mapping path asks the same ceiling
before pinning, refusing loudly instead of being OOM-killed.

Item 2 (state gates) found a real ABORT: ggml_backend_cuda_get_tensor_async (and the other three async
tensor entry points) asserted the PLAIN CUDA buffer type, so the batched prompt-cache save aborted as soon as
it touched a windowed KV.  Relaxed to ggml_backend_buft_is_cuda (the identity the scheduler itself gates on);
gate-state-pipe.sh and gate-ckpt-reuse.sh now pass on a windowed arm.

Three slide bugs, all found by the re-baseline:
* a COALESCED mapping straddling the spill boundary was flipped back whole by the next VRAM step, so the
  window spilled nothing while its warning claimed the tail was in system RAM.  Every mapping in a windowed
  region is now on the map-unit grid (grow_cells maps used_up, init_tensor commits up(W*nb1, unit), no
  coalescing) and a flip whose range is not exactly one mapping is refused loudly.
* cudaMemcpy into/out of a host-location mapping does not land on this driver (a 4 MiB restore completed and
  left zeros).  Every staging leg now goes through a device kernel copy, the access the probes measured
  working; LLAMA_KV_REGION_DEBUG=1 verifies each flip against its stage.
* rewriting one mapping as head/mid/tail loses the middle piece's bytes -- hence the grid invariant plus a
  refusal, not a cleverer flip.  The VMM selftest covers both halves.

OPEN (recorded in wip/kv-residency/A2-MIXED-BACKING.md §3.7.6): a 1-unit (4 MiB/tensor) spill on a 27B
changes the greedy text and shifts the prefill logits by KLD 0.004973, deterministically, while the flip is
byte-exact and a 4B arm with the same spill shape is byte-identical.  Purity may only be claimed for
non-spilling windowed arms until that is closed.

Not delivery work: nothing here is in patches/, release.json or any block.
